      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MEET ME AT THE BEACH NZ (4) went back last start then worked home in good style to score by a head at Gawler over 1609m, putting an end to a sequence of minor placings. Meets some better types this time but another win is on the cards. SEA HUNTER (9) is in good form with top-five finishes at his last four starts, most recently recording a third over 1800m at this track. Shouldn't spend a penny from this draw and the sprint lane may come in handy. Won't find this any harder and he can get the job done. WELL WELL (1) has been thereabouts of late and is a great chance to break through. Good effort last time out when he finished fourth at Gawler over 1609m. Top-three commodity from the pegs. JADES REASON (6) should be at her peak at the fifth run back from a spell, the latest outing a fifth at this venue a week ago. One for the exotics players.",
